  ('crested-butte-colorado', '12A', 'Crested Butte', 'United States', 'The last great Colorado ski town', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","hiking","romance","family"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Crested Butte = ''the last great Colorado ski town,'' end-of-the-road Victorian mining town at ~8,885 ft, surrounded by ~1.6 million acres of public land","Crested Butte Mountain Resort (Vail Resorts, Epic Pass) = birthplace of inbounds extreme skiing; ~37% expert terrain; Rambo ~55-degree pitch","~1,547 acres / 165 trails / 15 lifts / 2,787-ft vertical / 12,162-ft summit / 9,375-ft base at Mt. Crested Butte","Epic Pass (Vail Resorts) — alongside Vail, Beaver Creek, Breckenridge, Keystone","Colorado''s Wildflower Capital (1,500+ flowering species)","Crested Butte Wildflower Festival each July (2026 = 40th anniversary, ~10-19 Jul); peak bloom mid-Jul-early Aug","Gunnison Valley Health = area hospital (Level IV trauma, ~30 mi down-valley, clinics in Crested Butte/Mt. CB)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide)","hospital":"Gunnison Valley Health (Gunnison, 24/7 ER + Level IV trauma, ~30 mi down-valley; clinics in Crested Butte/Mt. CB); serious cases airlift to Denver Front Range trauma centres; backcountry via Crested Butte Search and Rescue / Gunnison County / 911","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (town ~8,885 ft, terrain 12,162 ft) — AMS risk, acclimatize/hydrate; EXTREME TERRAIN (Rambo ~55 deg — expert only, respect closures); AVALANCHE beyond ropes (check CAIC daily, guide + beacon/probe/shovel); tree wells + extreme cold/fast weather (valley among coldest in US); end-of-road remoteness (hospital ~30 mi); summer high-trail/14er/401-Trail lightning + exposure"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds, Feb) ski; summer Crested Butte Wildflower Festival (mid-July) + Jul