  ('mammoth-california', '12A', 'Mammoth Mountain', 'United States', 'California''s highest mountain, deepest snow, and longest season', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Pacific Coast', '{"ski","wellness","adventure","family","culinary","entertainment","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Mammoth = Alterra / Ikon (Alterra HQ Denver); CALIFORNIA''S HIGHEST ski resort (summit 11,053 ft, base 7,953 ft, ~3,100 ft vertical; town ~7,880 ft); a VOLCANIC lava-dome complex on the Long Valley Caldera","3,500+ acres, 175-178 trails (15% beg / 48% int / 37% adv), 25 lifts (~59,000/hr); ~400 in snow; no night skiing","ONE OF THE LONGEST SEASONS IN THE US: Nov-May typical, often into June, sometimes July - regularly the last major US resort open; distinctive long-spring demand window","Alterra also owns June Mountain (~1,500 ac, 41 trails, family-oriented) ~20+ mi N near June Lake","GENUINE natural hot springs in the Eastern Sierra (a real, rare ski-trip amenity): Benton Hot Springs confirmed (~135F source); Long Valley/Crowley springs widely known - Wellness is LIVE via the natural springs, NOT a hotel-spa claim","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: among CA''s biggest/most-visited but no per-resort count published - consensus only","Long haul: LA ~5 hr / Reno ~3 hr via US-395; Mammoth Yosemite Airport (MMH) ~7 mi E seasonal winter flights (weather-unreliable); TIOGA PASS (SR-120) CLOSED in winter -> Bay Area detour","NO on-site cat/heli (lift-served; regional guided touring only); VOLCANIC CO2 hazard near Horseshoe Lake; Hot Creek soaking PROHIBITED (dangerous geothermal); Ikon/lift prices dynamic"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Mammoth Hospital, Mammoth Lakes - small critical-access hospital, 24/7 ER (site 403''d - verify); larger Northern Inyo Hospital in Bishop (~40 mi S)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~7,953 ft GENUINELY HIGH, summit ~11,053 ft; SoCal drive market arrives sea-level - hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if AMS worsens); VOLCANIC CO2 (Horseshoe Lake ~170-ac tree-kill zone can hold lethal CO2 in depressions/snow-wells/cabins - avoid low pockets, heed signage); AVALANCHE backcountry - Eastern Sierra Avalanche Center (ESAC, esavalanche.org, ''eastside-region'' - VERIFY named sub-zones); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; tree-wells; US-395 winter driving + Caltrans chains + TIOGA PASS (SR-120) closed all winter; HOT CREEK soaking PROHIBITED (scalding/fluctuating geothermal - use only established safe springs)"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'' Week/Feb, powder weekends) - heavy SoCal drive-market demand","shoulder":"early season (Nov-mid Dec) + the long spring (Apr-May)","green":"deep summer bike-park/gondola season is its own draw; true lulls are late-spring weekdays + October","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Westin/Village 3-6 mo (holidays longer); regular winter 2-4 mo; SoCal drive market books holidays early","off_season_specials":"long spring skiing; summer bike park + Devils Postpile/Yosemite; festivals; midweek value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break; summer festivals (chamber music, reggae - verify dates)","campaign_start":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Ikon renewals + long-spring push; fire winter again Sep-Nov"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski California''s highest mountain","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"window dynamic; package best value","timing":"ski Nov-Jun","draw_rank":1,"hook":"an 11,053-ft summit over 3,500+ acres of open volcanic bowls — the biggest, highest ski experience in the state","si":"ski","blurb":"an 11,053-ft summit over 3,500+ acres of open volcanic bowls — the biggest, highest ski experience in the state","when":"ski Nov-Jun","commission":"DMC/ski-op 10-15% (embedded-capable)"},{"name":"Chase ~400 in