  ('park-city-utah', '12A', 'Park City', 'United States', 'America''s largest ski resort, rising out of a real', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","family","culinary","entertainment","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Park City Mountain = Vail Resorts / Epic; the LARGEST ski resort in the US by area (Park City + Canyons Village linked by the Quicksilver Gondola since the 2015 merger); ~7,300 acres marketed / 6,700 lift-served","Vertical 3,200 ft (base 6,900 / summit 10,026); 41 lifts, 324 runs; terrain 7% beg / 49% int / 44% adv; longest run Homerun 3.5 mi; ~355 in snow; no night skiing","A GENUINE 1880s silver-mining town (64 National-Register Main Street buildings) - not a built village; base ~6,900 ft = moderate altitude vs the CO/Cottonwood giants","Salt Lake City International (SLC) ~32-36 mi / ~35-45 min via I-80/Parley''s - the closest major airport to a major US resort","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: among the highest-volume US resorts (largest by area; town ~600k visitors) but no per-resort count published - consensus only","SUNDANCE Film Festival 22 Jan-1 Feb 2026 = the LAST Utah edition (relocates to Boulder CO 2027) - do NOT describe Park City as a Sundance host beyond 2026","Utah 2034 Winter Olympics awarded (10-26 Feb 2034); Park City Mountain hosts snowboard (halfpipe/slopestyle) + freestyle; Utah Olympic Park (2002 legacy) sliding/jumping","NO on-resort cat/heli - Park City Powder Cats is a SEPARATE Uinta snowcat op ~35 min (15,000+ private ac, ~$990-1,190/day); NO natural hot springs in town (Homestead Crater, Midway ~30 min); Epic/lift prices dynamic"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Park City Hospital (Intermountain Health) - 24/7 ER; higher-level trauma to SLC valley hospitals (~35-45 min via I-80); verify trauma level","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~6,900 ft moderate, summit ~10,026 ft - milder AMS risk; hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE backcountry (Park City ridgeline + Uintas) - Utah Avalanche Center (UAC) ''Salt Lake'' region (Uintas region for the Powder Cats backcountry) - VERIFY exact zone (UAC pages 403); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; tree-wells; cold + intense UV; I-80/Parley''s winter driving + UDOT traction (less canyon-closure risk than the Cottonwoods)"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, Sundance 22 Jan-1 Feb 2026, MLK, Presidents'', Feb-Mar); final Utah Sundance amplifies late-Jan","shoulder":"early season (late Nov-mid Dec), Jan midweek outside Sundance, April spring skiing","green":"May-Jun + Oct-Nov lull; summer Kimball Arts + biking + Utah Olympic Park","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Sundance + Canyons luxury 4-8 mo (Sundance lodging ~1 yr); regular winter 3-6 mo; spring 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"April spring-skiing; summer Kimball Arts + biking + Olympic Park; midweek value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, Sundance (22 Jan-1 Feb 2026, final Utah edition), MLK + Presidents'', spring break, Kimball Arts (summer - verify)","campaign_start":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Epic renewals + Sundance-farewell + luxury pre-book (Sundance far ahead); fire again Sep-Nov"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski the largest resort in America","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"window dynamic; package far better value","timing":"ski Nov-Apr","draw_rank":1,"hook":"~7,300 marketed acres across Park City and Canyons on one Epic pass, linked by the Quicksilver Gondola","si":"ski","blurb":"~7,300 marketed acres across Park City and Canyons on one Epic pass, linked by the Quicksilver Gondola","when":"ski Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC/ski-op 10-15% (embedded-capable)"},{"name":"Ride the Quicksilver Gondola between two mountains","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_ba